- **Pitch:** the couple's do-not-play list is a database where each song has 14 properties and a count of how often you played it anyway. The Cha Cha Slide is locked at 9:40 PM and can't be unlocked. AI summaries of guest requests mostly read "Mr. Brightside (again)." Plans are Ceremony ($0), Reception ($29/mo) and Open Bar ($1,950/yr, "A human who stands next to the uncle").
- **Design:** styled like a wedding invitation suite, in ivory, plum and gold. The fonts are Cormorant Infant for headings, Instrument Sans for body text and Great Vibes for script lines. None of the style, colours or fonts match the last 7 entries.
- **Images:** the three testimonial headshots passed review on the first try. The hero photo was dropped after two tries: the first had a garbled brand name on the DJ controller and the second had an Apple logo on the laptop. The hero is the typographic invitation card instead, and the social preview uses the studio logo.
- **Demo:** a workspace for one reception with a table and a board view, status filters and live search. Clicking a request opens a side panel where you can change its status and add comments. Every comment you post gets the reply "louder?" from the bride's mother. There's an AI summary button and a new-request form that merges duplicates. The run-of-show page lets you delay blocks, but the Cha Cha Slide never moves and its unlock button refuses with a different message each time.
- **Visual check:** I took one screenshot each of the landing page and the demo. Nothing was broken, so I made no edits.

